WEBVTT

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:18.640
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.030
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:45.980
And takes me

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:49.950
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:58.070
To the home of wind

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.450
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:44.010
Please come in!

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:57.320
Why are you so happy?

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:58.210
Because of that.

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:00.710
Those are my new clothes, aren't they?

00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:03.000
Because it's Sunday tomorrow.

00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:07.450
You've been doing something in secret
these few days in you're free time.

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:10.340
And I heard sewing sounds.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:14.020
I wanted to give you a surprise.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:16.950
Thank you, Marilla!

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:29.570
Well, how do you like them?

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:37.400
What's wrong?

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:41.040
I'll imagine that I like them.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:44.400
I don't want you to imagine it.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:48.490
Oh, I can see you don't like the dresses!

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:54.040
What is the matter with them?
Aren't they neat and clean and new?

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:55.280
Yes.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.200
Then why don't you like them?

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:03.150
They're... they're... not pretty.

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:05.060
Pretty!

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:09.660
I didn't trouble my head about
getting pretty dresses for you.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:16.840
I don't believe in pampering vanity, Anne.
I'll tell you that right off.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.840
Those dresses are good, sensible,
serviceable dresses,

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:22.200
without any frills or furbelows about them.

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:25.520
And they're all you'll get this summer.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.160
The gingham one and the blue
print will do you for school.

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:36.040
The sateen is for church and Sunday school.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:40.620
I'll expect you to keep them neat and clean.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.760
And not to tear them.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:50.100
I should think you'd be grateful
to get most anything

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:53.080
after those skimpy wincey
things you've been wearing.

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.740
Oh, I am grateful!

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:03.550
But I'd be ever so much gratefuller if you'd
made just one of them with puffed sleeves.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:08.190
Puffed sleeves are so fashionable now.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:13.520
It would give me such a thrill,
just to wear a dress with puffed sleeves.

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:16.510
Well, you'll have to do without your thrill.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:20.470
I hadn't any material to
waste on puffed sleeves.

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:25.150
I think they are
ridiculous-looking things anyhow.

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:30.100
I prefer the plain, sensible ones.

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:35.880
But I'd rather look ridiculous
when everybody else does,

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:39.400
than plain and sensible all by myself.

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:41.270
Trust you for that!

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:45.950
Well, hang those dresses
carefully up in your closet

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:49.230
and then sit down and learn
the Sunday school lesson.

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:54.290
Although the way you are now,
you'll be imagining about

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:56.620
puffed sleeves and forgetting to learn again.

00:04:57.010 --> 00:04:57.910
Definitely.

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:03.120
I don't want you to disgrace me

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:05.650
because you cannot answer tomorrow's
Sunday lessons.

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:23.610
I did hope there would be a
white one with puffed sleeves.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:32.060
I prayed for one, but I didn't much
expect it on that account.

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:38.180
I didn't suppose God would have time to
bother about a little orphan girl's dress.

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:42.840
I knew I'd just have to
depend on Marilla for it.

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:49.310
Well, fortunately I can imagine that
one of them is of snow-white muslin

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:52.650
with lovely lace frills and
three-puffed sleeves.

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:28.340
Good morning.

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:44.690
Your head still hurts?

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:47.730
A little. Don't worry about me.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:51.920
But Anne, you have to go
to Sunday school today.

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:55.470
I wanted to bring you to your first lesson,

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:59.470
but I didn't count on my
sickness worsening.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:02.240
What about Matthew?

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:05.710
Well now... I...

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:09.740
My brother hasn't gone to church for years.

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:13.110
He's always praying on the fields.

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:18.080
Well now, Anne shouldn't go alone.

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:20.660
Why not let her stay at home?

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:24.210
Matthew Cuthbert, what are you saying?

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:28.120
No. She must go to the church.

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:34.950
Alright. I'll go alone,
although is frightening, but

00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:38.860
maybe I can meet up with new friends.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:51.060
Are you alright?

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:51.880
Yes.

00:07:52.970 --> 00:07:54.550
They look good on you.

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:58.560
Here's a cent for collection.

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:01.560
You'll have to go down
and call for Mrs. Lynde.

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:04.260
She'll see that you get into the right class.

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:10.340
Now, mind you behave yourself properly.
Don't stare at people and don't fidget.

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:13.450
Right, I almost forgot.

00:08:14.030 --> 00:08:16.440
Bring a white box from the living room.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.870
I've bought you a new hat.

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:19.800
Hat?

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:09.480
Oh! So pretty!

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:56.750
What happened to Marilla?

00:09:57.610 --> 00:09:59.870
I told her there was a Women's Meet today,

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:02.610
and told her not to be late!

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:12.930
Good morning!

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:17.500
Thank you.

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:51.980
It's done.

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:56.910
Not even a decorative lace, it looked too simple.

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:08.830
I've become a wind blowing
towards the church.

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:36.050
Mrs. Rachel Lynde. Mrs. Lynde.

00:11:59.180 --> 00:12:03.260
Look. She's the girl miss Cuthbert adoped.

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:05.720
She came from the asylum it seems.

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:11.410
Look at that red hair, I hear
her temper was terrible.

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:13.970
I heard that she yelled at Mrs. Lynde.

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:18.590
No, she really insulted her, because
her temper is as bad as her hair.

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:22.580
But Jerry Buote said she talked all the
time to the trees and flowers.

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:24.690
That's very strange!

00:12:24.770 --> 00:12:26.160
Like a crazy girl.

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:28.710
Right. You can tell by looking at her hat.

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:30.840
Full of wild flowers and grass.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:44.910
Did you see her freckles?

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:46.620
I did.

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:48.540
They're so many.

00:13:37.390 --> 00:13:45.500
Almighty God, your love is

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:48.020
eternal.

00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:54.990
Your road is truth.

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:12.710
How rude.

00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:14.460
She really is strange.

00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:22.440
God, we should not be afraid,
we should praise the Almighty.

00:14:23.180 --> 00:14:30.300
Because you are the only existance
on this earth, and the only truth.

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:36.030
We walk in the way you guide us in.

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:45.230
Almighty God! We should praise...

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:52.820
God, thank you for it.

00:14:54.800 --> 00:14:57.120
Thank you for it, God.

00:15:16.580 --> 00:15:18.360
Then, you know how to cook?

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:20.910
What about sewing?

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:22.110
A little.

00:15:22.710 --> 00:15:23.910
Embroidery?

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:26.480
Knitting?

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:31.850
My sister knows all that.

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:05.070
I'm home Bonny.

00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:07.780
Were you lonely by yourself?

00:17:13.070 --> 00:17:14.560
Welcome back, Anne.

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:16.840
Marilla, are you alright now?

00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:19.930
How did you like Sunday school?

00:17:20.090 --> 00:17:22.750
I didn't like it a bit. It was horrid.

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:24.290
Anne Shirley!

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:28.420
I behaved well, just as you told me.

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:33.570
Mrs. Lynde was gone,
but I went right on myself.

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:37.320
All The other girls were looking at me
and whispering.

00:17:37.880 --> 00:17:40.750
Mr. Bell made an awfully long prayer.

00:17:41.110 --> 00:17:44.750
I would have been dreadfully
tired before he got through

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:46.780
if I hadn't been sitting by that window.

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:51.570
But it looked right out on the
Lake of Shining Waters,

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:56.050
so I just gazed at that and imagined
all sorts of splendid things.

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:59.960
You shouldn't have done anything of the
sort. You should have listened to Mr. Bell.

00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:05.390
But he wasn't talking to me.
He was talking to God.

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:08.970
I said a short prayer myself.

00:18:10.120 --> 00:18:14.970
There was a long row of white
birches hanging over the lake and the

00:18:14.970 --> 00:18:18.190
sunshine fell down through them,
way down, deep into the water.

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:25.120
It gave me a thrill and I just said,
"Thank you for it, God," two or three times.

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:28.470
Not out loud, I hope.

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:31.000
No, just under my breath.

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:34.060
I behave myself rather well.

00:18:35.060 --> 00:18:37.860
Good. And the class?

00:18:40.480 --> 00:18:43.030
There were nine other girls in it.

00:18:43.030 --> 00:18:45.630
They all had puffed sleeves.

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:51.200
I tried to imagine mine were
puffed, too, but I couldn't.

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:52.570
Why couldn't I?

00:18:54.760 --> 00:19:00.960
It was easy to imagine they were puffed
when I was alone in the east gable.

00:19:02.430 --> 00:19:09.060
But it was awfully hard there among
the others who had really truly puffs.

00:19:09.810 --> 00:19:13.110
You shouldn't have been thinking about
your sleeves in Sunday school.

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:15.100
You should have been attending to the lesson.

00:19:15.930 --> 00:19:18.420
I answered a lot of questions.

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:23.090
But the teacher asked ever so many. I don't
think it was fair for her to do all the asking.

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:25.910
There were lots I wanted to ask her.

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:29.000
Welcome back, Anne.

00:19:29.430 --> 00:19:30.200
I'm back.

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:34.250
So, did you meet any new friends?

00:19:34.490 --> 00:19:35.660
How could I?

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:36.970
What happened?

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:40.000
Didn't you go to make friends?

00:19:41.790 --> 00:19:43.910
But, I was unsuccessful.

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:48.390
Of course, friends don't come just like that.

00:19:49.510 --> 00:19:53.570
You two are not just kindred, you even
have personality similarities.

00:19:55.330 --> 00:19:57.200
Here comes the nagging old lady.

00:19:58.120 --> 00:19:59.690
I'd better turn in.

00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:05.000
I heard you weren't well.

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:08.810
I'm much better now.

00:20:09.370 --> 00:20:11.150
The true is, Marilla...

00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:16.790
that child did something strange
again, but I'm sure you were unaware.

00:20:17.130 --> 00:20:20.040
Something strange?
What did Anne do this time?

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:24.620
Her hat was rigged out ridiculous
with roses and buttercups.

00:20:24.830 --> 00:20:30.420
I thought I would sink through
the floor when I saw her.

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:33.530
Anne, did you do that to your hat?

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:38.940
I know pink and yellow
aren't becoming to me.

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:40.910
Becoming fiddlesticks!

00:20:41.460 --> 00:20:43.910
Ms. Lynde is referring to the fact of
you putting flowers on your hat.

00:20:43.910 --> 00:20:47.320
No matter what color they were,
that was ridiculous.

00:20:47.770 --> 00:20:51.410
I don't see why it's any more
ridiculous to wear flowers

00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:53.410
on your hat than on your dress.

00:20:53.780 --> 00:20:57.860
Lots of little girls there had bouquets pinned
on their dresses. What's the difference?

00:20:59.060 --> 00:21:01.610
Don't answer me back like that, Anne.

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:06.600
It was very silly of you to do such a thing.

00:21:06.600 --> 00:21:09.540
People will talk about it something dreadful.

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:13.510
So you should thank Mrs. Lynde
for coming here to let me know.

00:21:13.510 --> 00:21:16.350
You really know how to shame me.

00:21:17.660 --> 00:21:20.960
I'm sorry Marilla. I really am.

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:24.550
I never thought you'd mind.

00:21:25.190 --> 00:21:28.550
Lots of the little girls had artificial
flowers on their hats.

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:35.920
The roses and buttercups were so sweet and
pretty I thought they'd look lovely on my hat.

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:42.590
I'm afraid I'm going to be
a dreadful trial to you, Marilla.

00:21:43.300 --> 00:21:45.890
Maybe you'd better send me
back to the asylum.

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:50.150
That would be terrible.
I don't think I could endure it.

00:21:50.510 --> 00:21:55.150
Most likely I would go into consumption.
I'm so thin as it is.

00:21:56.070 --> 00:21:59.560
But that would be better
than being a trial to you.

00:21:59.810 --> 00:22:00.920
Be quiet, Anne!

00:22:02.160 --> 00:22:04.250
What nonsense is that?

00:22:04.890 --> 00:22:08.320
I don't want to send you back
to the asylum, I'm sure.

00:22:15.050 --> 00:22:16.350
Anne, wait!

00:22:42.160 --> 00:22:50.040
Marilla, Jerry Buote told me that
Diana's coming back tomorrow.

00:22:50.470 --> 00:22:52.690
Go tell Anne the news.

00:22:53.330 --> 00:22:56.150
Matthew, don't be such a busybody, please.

00:22:56.290 --> 00:23:02.580
Well now, but I feel that child would
get along well with Anne...

00:24:19.680 --> 00:24:23.550
Knowing a friend like Diana, would
boost Anne's self-confidence.

00:24:23.910 --> 00:24:26.740
Next of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:26.980 --> 00:24:28.360
A Solemn Vow and Promise

00:24:28.360 --> 00:24:29.160
Please watch!
